  "verbalization": "Vildagliptin is associated with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus through a chain of indications that link it to other drugs with similar mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Vildagliptin may be considered a potential repurposed therapy for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, as it shares a common pathway with other drugs like Gemigliptin, Teneligliptin, and Trelagliptin, which are all classified under the indication for Diabetes Mellitus. These drugs are typically used in the management of Type 2 Diabetes, and their shared indication implies a potential overlap in their therapeutic mechanisms. The presence of a direct indication from Vildagliptin to Diabetes Mellitus, along with the indirect indication through these other drugs, supports the hypothesis that Vildagliptin may have a role in the treatment of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering drug-class relationships and their mechanisms in the context of drug repositioning.",
